  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933611",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-11969",
      "knowledge_point_id": "af269509-92c0-5a82-b828-e8626f8e8eda",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Quotient Using Leibniz Notation",
      "problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{-x}{9-2x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u=-x$ and $v=9-2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(9-2x)\\cdot (-1)-(-x)\\cdot (-2)}{{(9-2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9+2x-2x}{{(9-2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{4x-9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{4x-9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{2x-9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
