    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-118350",
      "knowledge_point_id": "64edd709-3f6c-59e1-ae1f-bca25eca0483",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/a065146d50b16eade39c758b59e13994272cf7180aaa662008a1865e4160421e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/46e8f92e758c7f4643b64c05d0b457f7b99b6723ddf9be9cd63da28079b89618.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, compress it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ to give $y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
