    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-6761",
      "knowledge_point_id": "f71a8f16-93d4-5e5a-9b8b-e29efc682430",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Reflection of a Cosine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/4d660b71abd6c03c817b6cf18c5320a3f27d4fbf650f1ea032d27bf1652d3066.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/867ec8135efc671ea26c6691a9aef4803c35179b86b7af3b605c4b7d1d3a2498.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-cos⁡x.$",
      "answer_fields": [
