  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-118442",
      "knowledge_point_id": "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-48521ad98895",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine or Cosine Curve Over the Vertical Axis",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/997eb5cc08dcff78cb32f5b47b5d066546854b05f3b066953772e456e713d773.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could be used to describe the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/1e532c806d81c3c4015d78f814dc4ea3fc3483f22d34ade385894df2e8e7e3c5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=5sin⁡(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n5sin⁡(-x)=-5sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-5sin⁡x.$ However, $y=-5sin⁡x$ is not among the given options.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=\\frac{1}{5}sin⁡(-x)",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=sin⁡(-5x)",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=sin⁡(-\\frac{x}{5})",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=sin⁡(-x)-5",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=5sin⁡(-x)",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-118442",
        "kp_title": "Identifying the Reflection of a Sine or Cosine Curve Over the Vertical Axis",
        "kp_href": null
      },
      "topic_id": 259,
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/state.json",
