  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933833",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-48835",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data",
      "problem": "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(e)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(e)=\\frac{1}{e},\\,g(e)={e}^{2},\\,{g}^{′}(e)=2e\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=e.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=e$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=e} & =f(e){g}^{′}(e)+g(e){f}^{′}(e) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2e+{e}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{e} \\\\  & =3e.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3{e}^{2}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{2}{e}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2{e}^{2}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3e",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2e",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-48835",
        "kp_title": "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data",
        "kp_href": null
      },
